  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 14,
      "char_start": 936,
      "char_end": 1271,
      "text": "When at last, between ten and eleven o'clock one morning, she weighed\nanchor, and before a light north-westerly breeze, with her small sails\nset, glided out to sea, the quays were crowded with spectators, the\nmajority of the crew belonging to the place, and it being generally\nknown that they were bound on a longer voyage than usual"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 17,
      "char_start": 1259,
      "char_end": 1743,
      "text": "It was getting near bedtime, and she had been sitting half-asleep over\nthe fire, and perhaps her suddenly awakened excitement lent a more than\nusual animation and attraction to a pair of eyes and a face that would\nnowhere have passed unnoticed; for Carl Beck, who was at the head of the\nparty, seemed positively fascinated, and could not take his eyes off\nher, until, reddening with confusion, she instinctively stretched out\nher hand for her bodice, that lay beside her on the bench"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 18,
      "char_start": 1480,
      "char_end": 1804,
      "text": "\"\n\nThere was no scarcity of eatables, which were discussed amid a running\nfire of conversation upon every kind of topic; and then came the \"bowl,\"\na composition of various strong and spicy ingredients, of which Carl had\nthe secret, and which finally was lighted, and ladled into the glasses\nwhilst the blue flame was burning"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 19,
      "char_start": 266,
      "char_end": 585,
      "text": "Carl Beck was the life of the party; and very well he looked as he sat\nthere astride over the bench, with his glass in his hand, and his\nofficer's jacket with its anchor-buttons thrown open, and sang first one\nand then another of the rollicking drinking-songs that were then in\nvogue, the others joining in the chorus"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 20,
      "char_start": 1261,
      "char_end": 1610,
      "text": "The light from the fire fell upon his\nhandsome brown face, with the raven black curly hair, and the dark eyes\nthat it was said he had inherited from his recently deceased mother, who\nwas from Brest; and with his flow of animal spirits, that sufficed for\nthe whole party almost, he certainly was as manly and handsome a lad as\nyou would wish to meet"
    }
  ],
